    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1403">

                <pb facs="1513" n="1499" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.34112 RP/7–1244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-12T17:00:00-04:00">July 12, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received, 9:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>387. The Undersecretary of Foreign Relations<anchor n="76" xml:id="d1403-f1"/>
                    told me this morning that the President is interested in removing all the
                    quebracho properties in Paraguay from foreign control and that instructions are
                    being sent to Ambassador Velasquez to approach the Department with a view to an
                    Export Bank loan for purchasing them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1403-f1" n="76" xml:id="d1403-f1-content">
